## Run it

```sh
sh ./{{ bundle_filename }}
```

Or just double-click it in Finder. If you have already unpacked it, run the script inside the
folder instead:

```sh
./run_campaign.sh
```

That is the whole thing. It installs a pinned environment (via
[pixi](https://pixi.sh), downloading it first if you do not have it), generates the
target YAMLs, preflights them, runs Boltz-2, analyses the results, and writes
`{{ results_filename }}` next to itself.

Then upload that one file at **{{ site_url }}/auto/analysis** to explore it.

Safe to re-run at any point. Targets that already have a complete prediction are
skipped, so an interrupted campaign picks up where it stopped rather than starting over.

## What is in here

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `boltz_input.md` | Your campaign spec: proteins, partners, ligands, constraints. Editable. |
| `config.json` | The run settings you chose, machine-readable. Provenance only, not read at run time. |
| `run_campaign.sh` | The script above. Every setting is written out literally so you can read exactly what will run. |
| `pack_results.py` | Packs the finished campaign into `{{ results_filename }}`. |
| `BoltzMaker.py` | The pipeline itself. |
| `pixi.toml`, `pixi.lock` | The pinned environment: Boltz-2, RDKit, and the PLIP/OpenBabel/PyMOL analysis stack, locked for both macOS (Apple Silicon) and Linux (x86-64). |

## What it needs from your machine

- **A GPU, realistically.** CUDA on Linux or Apple Silicon's MPS. It will run on CPU, but
  slowly enough that it is only really useful for proving a campaign is valid.
- **Disk.** Several GB for the environment, plus Boltz-2's model weights.
- **The model weights are not in this bundle.** They are large and versioned by Boltz
  itself, so they download on first use and are cached in your home directory. A second
  campaign skips that step.

## If something goes wrong

The script stops on the first error and tells you which stage failed. A few common ones:

| Symptom | What it usually means |
|---|---|
| `pixi: command not found` after install | pixi went onto your PATH for future shells only. Run `source ~/.zshrc` or open a new terminal, then re-run. |
| Killed during prediction, no error | Out of memory. Lower **Parallel diffusion samples** or **Max MSA sequences**, or run fewer targets at once with **Only run the first N targets**. |
| A preflight check fails | The campaign spec has a real problem: an unparseable SMILES, a chain id over 5 characters, a missing referenced file. Fix `boltz_input.md` and re-run. |
| Some targets missing from the results | Those targets failed after their retries. The results file still carries everything that succeeded, and records the shortfall in its manifest. |

Full documentation: <https://github.com/bellcheddar/BoltzMaker>
